  "compiled_truth": "👨🏻‍🎓 ChatGPT for Education  - by Michael Spencer\n            \n            \n            \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n\n        \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n        \n\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n        \n            \n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n        \n          \n        \n        \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            AI Supremacy \n\nSubscribeSign inBenefactor 👨🏻‍🎓 ChatGPT for Education \n\nWhat people are saying. 📚✍🏼💡\n\nMichael SpencerJan 11, 2023∙ Paid8ShareImage credit: GPTZero website. \n\nHey Everyone, \n\n2023 is the best time to start a Substack as they have perfected the peer-driven discovery and audience retention features. Get away from algos and Ads and start publishing in your niche today!\n\nStart a Substack\n\nA lot of readers have expressed a going interest in ChatGPT’s impact on education. Here is a good resource to get you started: \n\ndocs.google.com/presentation/d…</a>\\n<span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\">#highered</span> <span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\">#edtech</span> <span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\">#chatgpt</span> <span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\">#education</span> <span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\">#teachered</span> <span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\">#k12</span> \",\"username\":\"torreytrust\",\"name\":\"Dr. Torrey Trust\",\"profile_image_url\":\"\",\"date\":\"Wed Jan 04 23:25:19 +0000 2023\",\"photos\":[{\"img_url\":\"https://pbs.substack.com/media/FlqivctXoAcE2Uc.png\",\"link_url\":\"https://t.co/VOyD7mSV2P\",\"alt_text\":\"Screenshots of the ChatGPT & education slide deck\"}],\"quoted_tweet\":{},\"reply_count\":0,\"retweet_count\":713,\"like_count\":2094,\"impression_count\":0,\"expanded_url\":{},\"video_url\":null,\"belowTheFold\":false}\" class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-12 pc-padding-16 pc-reset bg-primary-zk6FDl outline-detail-vcQLyr pc-borderRadius-md sizing-border-box-DggLA4 pressable-lg-kV7yq8 font-text-qe4AeH tweet-fWkQfo twitter-embed\">Dr. Torrey Trust@torreytrustChatGPT - what can it do? What can it NOT do? What can educators do? Learn more by browsing this open source slide deck. \ndocs.google.com/presentation/d…\n#highered #edtech #chatgpt #education #teachered #k12 11:25 PM · Jan 4, 2023713 Reposts · 2.09K LikesEducators are mixed on a world where Chatbots proliferate and can help students with Essays among other things. \n\nThe NYC Department of Education has banned the use of ChatGPT by students and teachers in New York City schools as there are serious concerns about its use hampering learning and leading to misinformation.\n\nThe ban was first reported by Chalkbeat, which confirmed the New York City Department of Education imposed it. The organization manages the largest school district in the U.S., so others might follow with similar decisions.\n\nGPTZero \n\nEdward Tian has created a tool to help discover if an essay was written by a person or an A.I. like ChatGPT and his main target audience is teachers, check it out: \n\nGPTZeroGPTZero Update v2Core Updates: Thank you for being one of the 10k+ people that have subscribed to this substack! The GPTZero.me website and landing page has been completely redesigned! We’re building a product with GPTZero technology for educators to use in their day-to-day workflow, that hopefully students will like too. Yesterday at midnight, we opened a sign up list fo…Read more3 years ago · 4 likes · 2 comments · Edward TianIf you are a Teacher or know someone who is please share this tool, it could help: \n\nShare\n\nEdward Tian@edward_the6I spent New Years building GPTZero — an app that can quickly and efficiently detect whether an essay is ChatGPT or human written12:17 AM · Jan 3, 20234.27K Reposts · 33.7K LikesJoin ChatZero Sign-up List for Educators\n\nThey also have a Facebook Group especially for teachers and educators. Clearly a lot of School and education workers are concerned about these tools and their potential impact on kids and prompt-engineering, cheating and so forth. \n\nHistorically some claim that ChatGPT is an “iPhone moment for A.I. adoption” and compare it with various historical precedents. For instance, the invention of the telephone in 1876 was met with simultaneous amazement and trepidation. Is Microsoft’s Bing Chatbot the same thing though? Widely expected to go live as early as this March. \n\nChatGPT’s role in education is a work in progress and there are currently many active disputes. \n\nContinue reading this post for free, courtesy of Michael Spencer.\n\nClaim my free postOr purchase a paid subscription.PreviousNext© 2026 Michael Spencer · Privacy ∙ Terms ∙ Collection notice Start your SubstackGet the appSubstack is the home for great culture\n        \n\n        \n            \n            \n        \n\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n\n        \n        \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n              